# D3.js v6 Tooltips and Interactions

## Overview
Tooltips provide hover information. Click interactions enable linked views between charts.

## Tooltip Implementation
```javascript
// Create tooltip div
const tooltip = d3.select("body").append("div")
  .attr("class", "tooltip")
  .style("opacity", 0)
  .style("position", "absolute")
  .style("background", "#fff")
  .style("border", "1px solid #ccc")
  .style("padding", "10px")
  .style("border-radius", "4px")
  .style("pointer-events", "none");

// Attach to elements
bubbles
  .on("mouseover", function(event, d) {
    tooltip.transition().duration(200).style("opacity", 0.95);
    tooltip.html(`<strong>${d.ticker}</strong><br/>Name: ${d.name}<br/>Sector: ${d.sector}`)
      .style("left", (event.pageX + 10) + "px")
      .style("top", (event.pageY - 28) + "px");
  })
  .on("mouseout", function() {
    tooltip.transition().duration(300).style("opacity", 0);
  });
```

## Click Interaction for Linked Views
```javascript
// Bubble click highlights table row
bubbles.on("click", function(event, d) {
  // Remove previous highlights
  d3.selectAll(".stock-row").classed("highlighted", false);
  d3.selectAll("circle").classed("selected", false);

  // Highlight this bubble
  d3.select(this).classed("selected", true);

  // Highlight corresponding table row
  d3.select(`#row-${d.ticker}`).classed("highlighted", true);

  // Scroll table row into view
  document.getElementById(`row-${d.ticker}`).scrollIntoView({
    behavior: "smooth", block: "nearest"
  });
});

// Table row click highlights bubble
d3.selectAll(".stock-row").on("click", function(event, d) {
  d3.selectAll(".stock-row").classed("highlighted", false);
  d3.selectAll("circle").classed("selected", false);

  d3.select(this).classed("highlighted", true);
  d3.select(`#bubble-${d.ticker}`).classed("selected", true);
});
```

## CSS for Interactions
```css
.tooltip {
  font-size: 13px;
  box-shadow: 2px 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);
  z-index: 1000;
}

circle.selected {
  stroke: #333;
  stroke-width: 3px;
}

tr.highlighted {
  background-color: #fff3cd !important;
}

circle {
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: stroke-width 0.2s;
}

circle:hover {
  stroke: #333;
  stroke-width: 2px;
}
```

# D3.js v6 CSV Data Loading and Parsing

## Overview
D3 v6 provides `d3.csv()` for loading and parsing CSV files. Returns a Promise.

## Basic CSV Loading
```javascript
// d3.csv returns a Promise
const data = await d3.csv("data/stock-descriptions.csv");
// or
d3.csv("data/stock-descriptions.csv").then(data => {
  // data is an array of objects, keys from header row
  console.log(data[0]); // {ticker: "AMZN", sector: "Information Technology", ...}
});
```

## Type Conversion
```javascript
const data = await d3.csv("data/stock-descriptions.csv", d => ({
  ticker: d.ticker,
  sector: d.sector,
  name: d["full name"],
  marketCap: d.marketCap ? +d.marketCap : null,
  country: d.country || null,
  website: d.website || null
}));
```

## Loading Multiple Files
```javascript
const [descriptions, priceData] = await Promise.all([
  d3.csv("data/stock-descriptions.csv"),
  d3.csv("data/indiv-stock/AAPL.csv")
]);
```

## Handling Missing Data
CSV fields that are empty become empty strings. Convert them properly:
```javascript
const marketCap = d.marketCap !== "" ? +d.marketCap : null;
const isETF = d.sector === "ETF";
```

## Notes for Local File Access
When opening HTML files directly (file:// protocol), d3.csv() may fail due to CORS.
Solutions:
- Embed data as inline JSON in the HTML
- Use a local server: `python3 -m http.server`
- Use fetch with appropriate headers

# Creating Data Tables with D3.js v6

## Overview
D3 can create and manage HTML tables dynamically from data arrays.

## Basic Table Creation
```javascript
function createTable(container, data, columns) {
  const table = d3.select(container).append("table")
    .attr("class", "stock-table");

  // Header
  const thead = table.append("thead").append("tr");
  thead.selectAll("th")
    .data(columns)
    .enter().append("th")
    .text(d => d.label)
    .on("click", (event, d) => sortTable(d.key));

  // Body
  const tbody = table.append("tbody");
  const rows = tbody.selectAll("tr")
    .data(data)
    .enter().append("tr")
    .attr("id", d => `row-${d.ticker}`)
    .attr("class", "stock-row");

  rows.selectAll("td")
    .data(d => columns.map(col => ({ value: col.format ? col.format(d[col.key]) : d[col.key], raw: d })))
    .enter().append("td")
    .text(d => d.value);

  return { table, tbody, rows };
}
```

## Column Definition
```javascript
const columns = [
  { key: "ticker", label: "Ticker Symbol" },
  { key: "name", label: "Full Company Name" },
  { key: "sector", label: "Sector" },
  { key: "marketCap", label: "Market Cap", format: formatMarketCap }
];
```

## Scrollable Table Container
```css
.table-container {
  max-height: 600px;
  overflow-y: auto;
  border: 1px solid #ddd;
}

.stock-table {
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
}

.stock-table th, .stock-table td {
  padding: 8px 12px;
  text-align: left;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;
}

.stock-table th {
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  background: #f8f9fa;
}
```

